WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.655
Running a restaurant means chasing orders.

00:00:02.726 --> 00:00:03.348
Calls.

00:00:03.348 --> 00:00:03.889
Chats.

00:00:03.889 --> 00:00:04.841
Paper slips.

00:00:04.841 --> 00:00:05.668
And somehow,

00:00:05.668 --> 00:00:07.489
the tomatoes are still missing.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.607
Suppliers live the same story.

00:00:10.607 --> 00:00:11.690
Orders from calls,

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.023
chats and paper.

00:00:13.074 --> 00:00:14.467
Stock on a clipboard.

00:00:15.361 --> 00:00:16.987
Supplify pulls it all into one

00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:17.698
line.

00:00:18.121 --> 00:00:18.783
One order,

00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:20.957
from first tap to final delivery.

00:00:21.341 --> 00:00:21.822
First,

00:00:21.822 --> 00:00:23.176
find your suppliers.

00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:25.295
Pick what you need.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.018
Build the order.

00:00:29.784 --> 00:00:30.274
Send it.

00:00:30.274 --> 00:00:30.969
Done.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.225
The supplier sees it the moment

00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:35.007
it lands,

00:00:35.007 --> 00:00:36.099
and accepts it.

00:00:36.941 --> 00:00:37.989
Checks the stock.

00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:39.260
The team picks and packs the

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.072
box.

00:00:41.161 --> 00:00:41.685
Loaded,

00:00:41.685 --> 00:00:42.719
and on its way.

00:00:44.861 --> 00:00:46.206
A driver takes it out,

00:00:46.206 --> 00:00:48.383
and every status update follows.

00:00:48.921 --> 00:00:51.080
The restaurant confirms what arrived.

00:00:52.661 --> 00:00:54.653
Restaurants, suppliers, drivers.

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:55.666
One network.

00:00:55.962 --> 00:00:56.790
Supplify.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.212
Every order, one line.

00:00:58.212 --> 00:01:00.105
Request a personal demo.
